# Keep Prettier focused on authored source rather than minified build output.
ai-prototypes/**/assets/**

# ...and the entry HTML those builds emit alongside them. This is the cause of
# the recurring "Prettier code formatter" CI failures: `assets/**` was ignored
# but `index.html` was not, so every time a prototype was rebuilt Vite wrote a
# fresh unformatted entry file and the next push failed the check. Formatting
# it is not a fix either -- the next build overwrites it and the failure comes
# straight back.
#
# The pattern is *.html rather than index.html, because a build can emit more
# than one entry file: Mirror's Vite config declares eight, so rebuilding it
# dropped chorus.html, reel.html and spotlight.html into the repo unformatted
# and the check failed again for exactly the reason this block already
# describes. Matching only index.html was the narrower version of the same bug.
#
# The negations below are the two entry files in here that are genuinely
# hand-authored rather than emitted, so they stay formatted like source. If a
# new prototype is authored by hand rather than built, add it here too.
ai-prototypes/*/*.html
!ai-prototypes/guise/index.html
!ai-prototypes/mimic/index.html
